      "repair": "The glazed barrel vault on the Glass Hall wing (hallGlass() in heidelberg-runtime-model.mjs, the 'glass' loft) was inside out: part() re-derives every normal from winding, and the vault's profile ran from +z over the crown to -z, which makes loft() wind its curved faces, flat base and end caps inward. From above, the vault was all back faces, so it read as see-through. The profile now runs from -z over the crown to +z (same points in the opposite order), so the vault faces out. The vertex set, the per-plane areas and the materials are unchanged; every vault plane's normal is reversed and its planar quads and caps are re-split (24 vault triangles). Because reviewed() drops faces pointing straight down at skyline level, the skyline LOD now omits the vault's hidden flat base instead of its crown (967 -> 965 triangles). Above-horizon see-through scan: 2.2% of the model before (window glass 66% of part), 0.13% after in source and all runtime LODs (skyline 2.0% -> 0.18%); the remainder is scattered sub-1% sandstone slivers that were already present.",
